# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings in the working copy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would check
# these out as CRLF. scripts/ops/*.sh are piped straight to a Linux host
# (`ssh <host> 'bash -s' < script`), and bash fails on the carriage returns
# with `$'\r': command not found`. The committed blob is already LF; this
# stops the checkout filter from breaking it.
*.sh text eol=lf
